; regression test: `pick`/exists-elim used to reject a perfectly valid witness whenever the
; existential's body contained *another* quantifier nested inside it. Root cause:
; `rename_all_vars` renames every bound variable (not just the outermost) to a fresh
; internal name when a formula is stored, so `exists x (forall y (R x y))`'s stored
; `simplified_expr` becomes `exists $$05 (forall $$06 (R $$05 $$06))`. `eval_pick`
; substitutes the witness for `$$05` and compares the result against the user's own
; literally-typed fact via `equal_expr` -- which used to be pure structural (token-by-token)
; equality, so `forall $$06 (R c $$06)` never matched the user's `forall y (R c y)`: same
; formula, different (internally generated) name for the nested bound variable. See
; doc/kurt-soundness.md #3.3.
load logic
bool R
arity R 2
use exists x (forall y (R x y))
pick c with forall y (R c y)
    true
true
